{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c56f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a074e4-2b36-7083-b248-59166c4be87c"},"sequence":274,"recorded_at":1780531400000543,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bfc095d2-89f8-42f0-9c2e-b6fe72e18de5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bfc095d2-89f8-42f0-9c2e-b6fe72e18de5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bfc095d2-89f8-42f0-9c2e-b6fe72e18de5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"f51c9b12-a5c1-48be-b272-55489b9957e0"},"task_id":"f51c9b12-a5c1-48be-b272-55489b9957e0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"f51c9b12-a5c1-48be-b272-55489b9957e0","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2z3se0/TASK-260830-2z3se0_review-verdict-rev5.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2z3se0 — reviewer verdict, CR revision 5\n2|\n3|- Verdict: **changes requested** → `to-dev`\n4|- repeat-of: `rev4/N8` (F2 — same prose-ahead-of-the-check shape, new instruments).\n5|  F1 and F3 are `none`.\n6|- Candidate tree `c0174e8761518432e55ed5bdcf915959da9bd9f4`, base\n7|  `1cb6b93585749df4ef4755ce93e486bcde9e3a6b`, verified equal to the worktree\n8|  before and after every probe (`git read-tree HEAD && git add -A && git write-tree`).\n9|\n10|## Gate results\n11|\n12|| Gate | Result |\n13|| --- | --- |\n14|| G-A — bound class over the production-derived denominator | **passes** |\n15|| G-A — zero/absent-fact class over the production-derived denominator | **passes** |\n16|| G-B — resurrections, and the 32 → 34 path delta | **passes** |\n17|| G-C — everything left open is stated | **fails** (F1, F2, F3) |\n18|\n19|Baseline before any mutant: `go build ./...` exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0,\n20|`gofmt -l internal/` clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 17/17 packages ok (29.7s).\n21|\n22|## What I measured myself\n23|\n24|262 narrowing mutants, each applied by byte-offset edit into production,\n25|PRESENT-asserted, driven through the **whole package suite**, restored with a\n26|sha256 comparison. Killers are classified: a failure whose only failing tests\n27|are the source-text censuses is recorded as `CENSUS_ONLY`, never as a kill.\n28|That distinction matters here — every identity mutant of the form\n29|`a != b` → `a != b && a != \"\"` adds a derived row and reddens\n30|`TestIdentityGatesAreCensused` on its own.\n31|\n32|| Battery | applied | behavioural kills | survived | census-only | compile-fail |\n33|| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n34|| `require*` both edges, all 19 call sites | 35 | 33 | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n35|| `check*` every literal edge (68 edges) | 68 | 60 | 8 | 0 | 0 |\n36|| `len` guards in `if` conditions + tuple/env rows | 22 | 19 | 1 | 2 | 0 |\n37|| identity NEQ, both sides of all 62 derived rows | 119 | 73 | 0 | 34 | 12 |\n38|| `==`-spelled refusal gates (outside both censuses) | 13 | 10 | 0 | 3 | 0 |\n39|| typed re-runs of the 5 above that needed real types | 5 | 3 | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n40|| **total** | **262** | **198** | **13** | **39** | **12** |\n41|\n42|### G-A, bound class — closed\n43|\n44|The brief's specific worry was that `requireStringBounds` callers might be\n45|pinned individually while the wrapper stays unmeasured. Both readings are\n46|answered: **all 19 `require*` call sites are driven at both edges**, and every\n47|finite edge dies.\n48|\n49|- 16 minimum edges (`1` → `0`) — 16 killed.\n50|- 17 finite maximum edges (`N` → `N+1`) — 17 killed.\n51|- 2 `maxUint53` maxima (`maxUint53` → `maxUint53+1`) — survived, and **correctly\n52|  stated**: `parseUint53Literal` (decode.go:225) refuses any literal above\n53|  `maxUint53` during parsing, so no input reaches the widened band. The registry\n54|  rows say exactly this and `TestUint53RepresentabilityCeiling` proves the\n55|  mechanism at `rawUint53` and `checkUint53Bounds`.\n56|\n57|Across the 68 `check*` literal edges plus the 19 `len` guards, 79 of 90 died.\n58|All 11 survivors trace to a committed row, and I verified each rationale rather\n59|than accepting it:\n60|\n61|- 3 × `manifest.go:185` platforms (element min, element max, count max) —\n62|  registry says \"unreachable behind `scalar.ParsePlatform` and the four-name\n63|  closed set\". True: `manifest.go:192-201` runs every element through\n64|  `scalar.ParsePlatform`, which refuses everything outside\n65|  `macos|linux|wsl2|windows`, `\"\"` included, and a fifth distinct member does\n66|  not exist. The row's wording names element 16 and count 4; the element\n67|  *minimum* is equally unreachable but is not spelled out.\n68|- 5 × `65536` count ceilings (`canonical_event_ids`,\n69|  `canonical_event_candidate_ids`, `raw_reference_ids`,\n70|  `required_source_object_ids`, `created_resource_keys`) — stated bound,\n71|  65537-element body.\n72|- 1 × `decode.go:441` `len(name) < 3` → `< 2` — registry says no 2-character key\n73|  satisfies the reverse-DNS grammar. Correct.\n74|- 1 × `protocol.go:527` `len(trimmed) == 0` — rostered plumbing, a trim helper\n75|  with no refusal. Correct.\n76|- 1 × `tuple.go` caller-side `environment.EnvironmentID` — the entry side dies\n77|  (`TestTupleAdmissionZeroFactsRefuse`); the caller side is the documented\n78|  hand-built-caller-param bound.\n79|\n80|**No unstated bound survivor.**\n81|\n82|### G-A, zero/absent-fact class — closed\n83|\n84|Over the 62 derived rows I generated 119 mutants (both operands of every\n85|reachable row) and completed the 4 rows my generator could not type\n86|(`count != 1`, `occurrences != 1`, `context.Environment != admitted`,\n87|`entry.Key.Environment != environment`) with hand-typed equivalents.\n88|\n89|**54 of 54 driven rows produce at least one behavioural kill.** Zero survivors.\n90|Zero of the 8 exempt rows was killed by my battery, so no row is exempted that\n91|a test would in fact catch.\n92|\n93|The 34 `CENSUS_ONLY` results are all one of: an exempt row behaving as declared;\n94|a side that is a package constant (`ProtocolID`, `probeSchemaVersion`,\n95|`\"accepted\"`, `\"archive_only\"`, `capabilityOrder[index]`) where the added clause\n96|can never fire; a side already refused by an earlier gate in the same function;\n97|or the stated hand-built-caller-param bound. None is an unmeasured fact side.\n98|\n99|### G-B — resurrections and the 32 → 34 delta\n100|\n101|Reconstructing the rev4 tree from its committed patch\n102|(`1469c6348e064454dd31a5a727e25486ed467b1b`) and diffing it against the rev5\n103|candidate:\n104|\n105|```\n106|git diff 1469c634 c0174e87 -- '*.go' ':(exclude)*_test.go'   # empty\n107|```\n108|\n109|**Zero production bytes changed between rev4 and rev5.** Resurrection is\n110|impossible by construction, and my 262 mutants re-measure the same production\n111|the rev4 battery measured. The delta is `LOGBOOK.md` (+9), the two new census\n112|files (+2072), `inventory_test.go` (+117 for N8), and the two rewired tripwires\n113|(±4 each). 32 → 34 = `bound_census_test.go` + `identity_census_test.go`.\n114|\n115|The two tripwire rewires strengthen rather than weaken: `TestStringBoundEdges`\n116|and `TestEnvelopeEchoEmptyStringRefuses` now take their expected row count from\n117|the registry instead of a frozen literal, so a new registry row forces a new\n118|driver row.\n119|\n120|N8 is genuinely fixed. Planting `var zzNewFault = axerror.New` reddens\n121|`TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction` with the indirection sentence at the\n122|planted position.\n123|\n124|## Findings\n125|\n126|### F1 — the identity census derives only `!=`, and two live zero-fact gates are spelled `==`\n127|\n128|`scanIdentityGateIDs` (identity_census_test.go:66) matches `token.NEQ` only. The\n129|file's own sentence is unqualified: *\"A new identity gate with no row fails the\n130|census.\"* It does not.\n131|\n132|`discovery.go:105` and `discovery.go:112` are zero-fact refusals in the exact\n133|class this leaf has reworked for four rounds, written the other way:\n134|\n135|```go\n136|if candidate.ExecutablePath == \"\" { ... failInvalid(\"discovery candidate carries no executable path\") }\n137|if candidate.OwnerIdentity  == \"\" { ... failInvalid(\"discovery candidate carries no owner identity\") }\n138|```\n139|\n140|Neither is in the 62. Both are behaviourally covered today —\n141|`TestDiscoverRefusals` kills a narrowing of each — so nothing is currently\n142|uncovered. The gate is what fails: an added production file containing\n143|\n144|```go\n145|func zzProbeEqualityRefusal(observed, expected string) error {\n146|    if observed == expected { return nil }\n147|    return json.Unmarshal(nil, nil)\n148|}\n149|```\n150|\n151|passes the entire package suite unrostered. The control plant confirms the\n152|probe is fair: the same file written as `if observed != expected` reddens\n153|`TestIdentityGatesAreCensused` naming the planted site.\n154|\n155|Either extend the denominator to `==`-spelled refusals — starting with the two\n156|live `discovery.go` rows and their existing drivers — or narrow the sentence and\n157|declare the spelling as a stated bound naming those two sites.\n158|\n159|### F2 — the bound census has the N8 blind spot that was fixed for the constructor census in this same commit\n160|\n161|`repeat-of: rev4/N8.`\n162|\n163|`scanBoundSiteIDs` (bound_census_test.go:126-131) takes `call.Fun.(*ast.Ident)`\n164|and returns early on anything else, and its `len`-guard pass walks `*ast.IfStmt`\n165|conditions only. Its sentence is likewise unqualified: *\"A new bound with no row\n166|fails the census.\"*\n167|\n168|Three token-preserving plants, each added to production and run through the full\n169|suite, are invisible:\n170|\n171|| plant | suite |\n172|| --- | --- |\n173|| `var zzprobeIndirect = requireStringBounds` + `zzprobeIndirect(members, \"zz_probe_member\", 1, 4096)` | green |\n174|| `return len(value) >= 1 && len(value) <= 512` (bound in a `return`, not an `if`) | green |\n175|| `for i := 0; len(values) > 128 && i < 1; i++` (bound in a `for` condition) | green |\n176|\n177|The first is literally the N8 shape. rev4 asked for it, the producer built\n178|`isAxerrorNew` + `parentNode` indirection detection for the constructor census\n179|this round, and then shipped a new census with the same hole. The fix already\n180|exists in `inventory_test.go` and needs porting to the six bound helpers.\n181|\n182|This is a durability finding, not a coverage one: I verified the current\n183|denominator is complete for today's source. An independent any-call-shape scan\n184|of the package finds exactly **58** calls to the six helpers, and the census\n185|derives **58**. The only `len` comparisons outside an `if` condition are six\n186|loop indices (`index < len(...)` in decode.go ×4, tuple.go ×2), none of them a\n187|domain bound. Nothing is unmeasured today; the instrument that two more leaves\n188|inherit is what fails open.\n189|\n190|Either widen the derivation (indirection for the six helpers, `len` guards in\n191|`switch`/`for`/`return`/assignment contexts) or narrow both sentences and state\n192|the bound.\n193|\n194|### F3 — unstated survivor: the capability-usability status clause\n195|\n196|```go\n197|// probe.go:469\n198|func CapabilityUsable(probe Probe, name string) bool {\n199|    value, present := probe.Capabilities[name]\n200|    if !present { return false }\n201|    return value.Status == \"available\" && value.Enabled\n202|}\n203|// probe.go:534 capabilityMapUsable — identical body over a raw map\n204|```\n205|\n206|Narrowing the status clause to also admit `capabilityStatuses[1]`\n207|(`\"conditional\"`) — no new literal, no new `!=`, so no census fires — leaves the\n208|**full package suite green** at both sites. These are authorization predicates:\n209|`capabilityMapUsable` is the whole of `CheckTargetWriteGates` at probe.go:497\n210|and :505, and `CapabilityUsable` gates the doctor required-capability check at\n211|probe.go:693.\n212|\n213|I believe it is equivalent, and I checked why rather than assuming:\n214|`decodeCapabilityValue` refuses `enabled=true` with a non-`available` status\n215|(probe.go:114), and `TestCapabilityStatusMatrix` drives all eight\n216|status × enabled combinations through `DecodeProbe`. So no probe produced by the\n217|decoder can carry `conditional`+`enabled`. But `CapabilityUsable` is exported\n218|and takes a caller-built `Probe`, the two functions appear in the identity\n219|census only as *presence-default* rows (`outcome: false` when absent, driver\n220|`TestCapabilityUsableAbsentIsNotUsable`), and the equivalent list in the rework\n221|note covers `decodeCapabilityValue`'s own `status != \"available\"` echo — not\n222|this clause.\n223|\n224|That makes it exactly the shape G-C names: a survivor with no stated bound. It\n225|needs one row or one comment naming the upstream coherence gate, or a drive of a\n226|hand-built `Probe{Capabilities: {\"x\": {Status: \"conditional\", Enabled: true}}}`\n227|through `CheckTargetWriteGates`.\n228|\n229|Lineage note, so routing is not misled: rev3/B4 named these same two functions\n230|and closed their **absence** path (`TestCapabilityUsableAbsentIsNotUsable`, and\n231|the rows in the presence census). This is their **status** clause, a different\n232|class, so I record `repeat-of: none` rather than a fourth round on the\n233|zero/absent-fact class. It is adjacency, not recurrence.\n234|\n235|## Explicitly closed — do not re-litigate in round 6\n236|\n237|- The bound class over its production-derived denominator. 122 mutants,\n238|  110 behavioural kills, 12 survivors all traced to a committed row whose\n239|  rationale I verified against the code.\n240|- The zero/absent-fact class over its production-derived denominator.\n241|  54 of 54 driven rows behaviourally killed; 8 of 8 exemptions consistent.\n242|- Both censuses fail closed on the shapes they do cover (control plant reddens\n243|  both, naming the planted sites).\n244|- N8, the constructor-census indirection.\n245|- Resurrections: none possible; production is byte-identical to rev4.\n246|- README/traceability: acceptance cases 81 → 88, the 7 session-adapter cases\n247|  name real committed tests, and the README states the Section 7.8 clause\n248|  binding stays `unevidenced` rather than claiming clause coverage. Honest.\n249|\n250|## Reproduction\n251|\n252|```bash\n253|# tree identity\n254|git read-tree HEAD && git add -A && git write-tree     # c0174e87…\n255|\n256|# rev4 → rev5 production delta (empty)\n257|git diff 1469c634 c0174e87 -- '*.go' ':(exclude)*_test.go'\n258|\n259|# F1 / F2 plants: add the probe file to internal/sessadapter, then\n260|go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -count=1\n261|\n262|# control plant (must redden both censuses)\n263|#   func zzControlBound(m map[string]json.RawMessage) error {\n264|#       return requireStringBounds(m, \"zz_control_member\", 1, 4096) }\n265|#   func zzControlIdentity(a, b string) bool { if a != b { return false }; return true }\n266|\n267|# F3\n268|#   probe.go:469 / :534  value.Status == \"available\"\n269|#     -> (value.Status == \"available\" || value.Status == capabilityStatuses[1])\n270|go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -count=1     # green\n271|```"}}}
