indirection detection for the constructor census\n179|this round, and then shipped a new census with the same hole. The fix already\n180|exists in `inventory_test.go` and needs porting to the six bound helpers.\n181|\n182|This is a durability finding, not a coverage one: I verified the current\n183|denominator is complete for today's source. An independent any-call-shape scan\n184|of the package finds exactly **58** calls to the six helpers, and the census\n185|derives **58**. The only `len` comparisons outside an `if` condition are six\n186|loop indices (`index < len(...)` in decode.go ×4, tuple.go ×2), none of them a\n187|domain bound. Nothing is unmeasured today; the instrument that two more leaves\n188|inherit is what fails open.\n189|\n190|Either widen the derivation (indirection for the six helpers, `len` guards in\n191|`switch`/`for`/`return`/assignment contexts) or narrow both sentences and state\n192|the bound.\n193|\n194|### F3 — unstated survivor: the capability-usability status clause\n195|\n196|```go\n197|// probe.go:469\n198|func CapabilityUsable(probe Probe, name string) bool {\n199|    value, present := probe.Capabilities[name]\n200|    if !present { return false }\n201|    return value.Status == \"available\" && value.Enabled\n202|}\n203|// probe.go:534 capabilityMapUsable — identical body over a raw map\n204|```\n205|\n206|Narrowing the status clause to also admit `capabilityStatuses[1]`\n207|(`\"conditional\"`) — no new literal, no new `!=`, so no census fires — leaves the\n208|**full package suite green** at both sites. These are authorization predicates:\n209|`capabilityMapUsable` is the whole of `CheckTargetWriteGates` at probe.go:497\n210|and :505, and `CapabilityUsable` gates the doctor required-capability check at\n211|probe.go:693.\n212|\n213|I believe it is equivalent, and I checked why rather than assuming:\n214|`decodeCapabilityValue` refuses `enabled=true` with a non-`available` status\n215|(probe.go:114), and `TestCapabilityStatusMatrix` drives all eight\n216|status × enabled combinations through `DecodeProbe`. So no probe produced by the\n217|decoder can carry `conditional`+`enabled`. But `CapabilityUsable` is exported\n218|and takes a caller-built `Probe`, the two functions appear in the identity\n219|census only as *presence-default* rows (`outcome: false` when absent, driver\n220|`TestCapabilityUsableAbsentIsNotUsable`), and the equivalent list in the rework\n221|note covers `decodeCapabilityValue`'s own `status != \"available\"` echo — not\n222|this clause.\n223|\n224|That makes it exactly the shape G-C names: a survivor with no stated bound. It\n225|needs one row or one comment naming the upstream coherence gate, or a drive of a\n226|hand-built `Probe{Capabilities: {\"x\": {Status: \"conditional\", Enabled: true}}}`\n227|through `CheckTargetWriteGates`.\n228|\n229|Lineage note, so routing is not misled: rev3/B4 named these same two functions\n230|and closed their **absence** path (`TestCapabilityUsableAbsentIsNotUsable`, and\n231|the rows in the presence census). This is their **status** clause, a different\n232|class, so I record `repeat-of: none` rather than a fourth round on the\n233|zero/absent-fact class. It is adjacency, not recurrence.\n234|\n235|## Explicitly closed — do not re-litigate in round 6\n236|\n237|- The bound class over its production-derived denominator. 122 mutants,\n238|  110 behavioural kills, 12 survivors all traced to a committed row whose\n239|  rationale I verified against the code.\n240|- The zero/absent-fact class over its production-derived denominator.\n241|  54 of 54 driven rows behaviourally killed; 8 of 8 exemptions consistent.\n242|- Both censuses fail closed on the shapes they do cover (control plant reddens\n243|  both, naming the planted sites).\n244|- N8, the constructor-census indirection.\n245|- Resurrections: none possible; production is byte-identical to rev4.\n246|- README/traceability: acceptance cases 81 → 88, the 7 session-adapter cases\n247|  name real committed tests, and the README states the Section 7.8 clause\n248|  binding stays `unevidenced` rather than claiming clause coverage. Honest.\n249|\n250|## Reproduction\n251|\n252|```bash\n253|# tree identity\n254|git read-tree HEAD && git add -A && git write-tree     # c0174e87…\n255|\n256|# rev4 → rev5 production delta (empty)\n257|git diff 1469c634 c0174e87 -- '*.go' ':(exclude)*_test.go'\n258|\n259|# F1 / F2 plants: add the probe file to internal/sessadapter, then\n260|go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -count=1\n261|\n262|# control plant (must redden both censuses)\n263|#   func zzControlBound(m map[string]json.RawMessage) error {\n264|#       return requireStringBounds(m, \"zz_control_member\", 1, 4096) }\n265|#   func zzControlIdentity(a, b string) bool { if a != b { return false }; return true }\n266|\n267|# F3\n268|#   probe.go:469 / :534  value.Status == \"available\"\n269|#     -> (value.Status == \"available\" || value.Status == capabilityStatuses[1])\n270|go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -count=1     # green\n271|```","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
